.TH man 1 "2026-11-19" "0.20.0" "Profanity XMPP client"

.SH NAME
/plugins

.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage plugins. Plugins are searched for in global and user XDG directories.
 Use 'load' and 'unload' to run plugins for the current session only. Use 'enable' and 'disable' to configure plugins to auto-load on startup. Running '/plugins' without arguments displays active and available plugins.

.SH SYNOPSIS
/plugins

.LP
/plugins install <path|URL>

.LP
/plugins load [<plugin>]

.LP
/plugins unload [<plugin>]

.LP
/plugins enable <plugin>

.LP
/plugins disable <plugin>

.LP
/plugins uninstall <plugin>

.LP

.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
\fBinstall <path|URL>\fR
.RS 4
Copy a local .lua file or directory, or download from URL into the user plugins directory.
.RE
.PP
\fBload [<plugin>]\fR
.RS 4
Load a plugin into the current session only. Passing no argument loads all available plugins.
.RE
.PP
\fBunload [<plugin>]\fR
.RS 4
Unload a plugin from the current session. Passing no argument unloads all loaded plugins.
.RE
.PP
\fBenable <plugin>\fR
.RS 4
Enable a plugin to autoload on start and load it into the active session.
.RE
.PP
\fBdisable <plugin>\fR
.RS 4
Disable a plugin from autoloading on start and unload it.
.RE
.PP
\fBuninstall <plugin>\fR
.RS 4
Unload, disable, and remove a plugin from the user plugins directory.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
/plugins

.LP
/plugins install https://profanity-im.github.io/example.lua

.LP
/plugins install /home/user/example.lua

.LP
/plugins load example.lua

.LP
/plugins unload example.lua

.LP
/plugins enable sounds.lua

.LP
/plugins disable sounds.lua

.LP
/plugins uninstall sounds.lua

.LP
